WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:10.640
While Huawei and ZTE have been rightly targeted&nbsp;
by the US government for their security risks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:15.440
another highly concerning Chinese tech company&nbsp;
has made considerable inroads in American homes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:20.960
and businesses. Tuya is the world's leading&nbsp;
company in the internet of things, or IOT,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:27.120
sector. Tuya's technologies power more than 100&nbsp;
million smart devices around the world, including&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:31.840
consumer products, surveillance equipment, and&nbsp;
manufacturing and supply chain applications.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:37.760
One cyber security firm's investigation found that&nbsp;
Tuya-powered devices may be funneling sensitive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:43.680
data to Beijing. Chinese law requires Tuya to&nbsp;
give its data to the Chinese government without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:50.240
reporting this disclosure. Conceivably the PRC&nbsp;
could also use Tuya's vast reach to manipulate or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:55.440
hack critical American infrastructure, imperiling&nbsp;
large swaths of our just-in-time economy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.960
There are ready alternatives to Tuya in America&nbsp;
and other trusted countries. It's time to cut&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.600
off the unnecessary risk that Tuya poses, and bar&nbsp;
the company from operating in the United States.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:12.240
What do you think? Should the US government more&nbsp;
aggressively scrutinize Chinese tech companies?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:16.320
Let us know in our poll. Also, let us know&nbsp;
what other topics you'd like our scholars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:21.600
to cover in 60 seconds, and be sure to like and&nbsp;
subscribe for more research and videos from AEI.

